        <body>
            <div xml:id="d370">

                <pb facs="0563" n="469" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg469"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. McDonald to Mr. Olney.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Teheran, Persia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-01-23"><hi rendition="#italic">January 23, 1896</hi></date>.
                        (Received Feb. 28.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 224, Dip. Ser.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Herewith I forward copies of telegrams
                    received at this legation from Dr. Cochran and Mr. Howard at Oroomiah,
                    requesting a guard to bring the American missionaries from Van, Turkey. Of
                    course I could furnish no guard beyond the border. Neither could the Persian
                    Government. It would have been simply invasion. Therefore I sent the answer
                    inclosed.</p>
                <p>It may be proper to add that I was informed by the Persian officials that these
                    refugees would be under armed protection from the time they crossed the
                    border.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alex. McDonald.</hi></signed></closer>




